1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,867
This research site brings source material,
comparison notes, and export tools into one
place.

2
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:15,700
Start with the curated John 1 preset. The
worksheet names its sources and labels editorial
notes.

3
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:22,333
Each edition is named. You can inspect the
readings and the notes that explain them.

4
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:30,867
The raw Markdown makes the handoff visible.
Review the source boundary and research prompts
before downloading.

5
00:00:30,867 --> 00:00:37,400
Download the dossier as a Markdown file. Then
upload it to NotebookLM.

6
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:44,333
The companion audio prompt asks the hosts to
distinguish source text from interpretation.

7
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:55,867
Data preparation. Workflow design. A handoff
people can inspect. Explore the site and
engineering case study at the links in this post.
